WEBVTT

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:12.340
Arashi!

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.930
-Arashi!
-Arashi!

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:16.930
-Arashi!
-Arashi!

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.180
-Arashi!
-Arashi!

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.350
-Arashi!
-Arashi!

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.100
-Arashi!
-Arashi!

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:24.390
A towel?

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:41.120
Accidents aren't just coincidental
if they keep happening.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.830
Misfortune? I don't think
that's the right way to put it.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.420
It's more like... Well...

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.930
Sorry, boys.

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:59.600
I hate doing this kind of thing.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.390
Don't either of them have
any casual clothes?

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:06.270
What?

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:07.270
What's this?

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.030
You do realize this is our room, right?

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.000
VERNAL EQUINOX

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:50.580
Are collecting model guns your hobby?

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.960
You even have a maintenance kit.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.590
Your parents were awfully nice
to include it in your pack.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.090
What are you here for?

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:01.970
Do you remember how you told us
that you had gunpowder?

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.600
I just thought it might be dangerous
if you weren't storing it properly.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.180
We're taking good care of it.

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.020
Handing it over to you people
would be much more dangerous.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.560
I suppose that's true.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.190
Then I'll trust you with it.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.440
Sorry for coming in without permission.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.150
Wait.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.030
You haven't stolen anything, have you?

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:21.820
Of course not.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:23.280
Do you want to check?

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:29.830
No, forget it.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.410
What is that?

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.370
Just a pendant.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:34.540
Bye, then.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:43.430
What happened?

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:44.720
Beats me.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.300
Having fun with women again?

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:47.970
Cut it out.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:52.270
I guess being wary of newcomers is
the responsible thing to do.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:55.730
We don't have anything to hide, though.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:01.280
That was a real gun.

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.160
But why?

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:08.200
Why do those boys have guns?

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.700
<i>You want to know if you can have guns?</i>

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:16.080
Yes. Would it be permissible for us
to go armed?

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:19.920
We plan on equipping everyone
with a knife, of course.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:22.590
But guns are a delicate subject.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:25.970
The opinions of the staff are divided.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:31.640
Ms. Saotome, if you would like to
bring a gun, I'll allow it.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:36.520
In America or other countries,
I imagine all members get a rifle.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:41.780
In other words, you're saying that
some people in the future will have them.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:44.650
There are other plans
aside from the 7SEEDS Project.

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:49.870
And some from the government want to
leave behind many guns and other weapons.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.700
I'm not sure I agree with that idea.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:53.200
I feel the same.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:58.000
It's not a weapon, but we will be giving
all the guides a neurotoxin,

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:00.210
potassium cyanide, for suicide.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.550
In the event that there is no hope
for survival in the future,

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:10.050
or if all members are stricken ill
and desire an easy way out, then...

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.810
That is a heavy responsibility.

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:17.600
It can be used to commit suicide
or to kill unstable members of the group.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:22.030
Please make sure it's safe,
so it's not stolen and used for wrong.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:23.610
Understood, sir.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:29.240
However, potassium cyanide can lose
its toxicity depending on how it's stored.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:32.790
You might not be able to
actually use it in the future.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:36.580
Just like the short story
<i>A Slice of Bread</i>?

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:40.340
The one where the bread was actually
a piece of wood.

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:41.290
By the way,

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:44.670
will I be receiving a list of names
for the other teams?

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.220
No.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.640
But if you come across
any of the other teams,

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:51.600
please watch after them.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.980
He never said for certain
that guns wouldn't be allowed.

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:01.610
Who are those boys?

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:08.950
This can be used both to commit suicide
and to kill others.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:15.500
<i>Arashi...</i>

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:18.330
<i>What if we don't find him?</i>

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.920
Arashi is a really good swimmer.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:22.960
He'll probably head for the coast.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:28.670
If he can at least light a fire,
then we can spot it when it gets dark.

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:30.800
This is unusual.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:32.850
It's starting to get foggy.

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:39.480
<i>It's freezing.</i>

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:41.600
<i>There's a ringing in my ears.</i>

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:43.310
<i>I'm alone.</i>

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.150
<i>I'm so very alone.</i>

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:52.570
<i>Ever since I came to this world,
Natsu and Semimaru have been by my side.</i>

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.580
<i>When I was feeling down...</i>

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:58.250
<i>and when I had fallen into despair...</i>

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:00.290
<i>They were there.</i>

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:03.670
<i>It was so reassuring.</i>

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:05.710
TALENT SHOW

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.170
<i>What are you all doing now?</i>

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:09.670
<i>I'm so sorry to make you worry.</i>

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:13.510
<i>It's cold. So very cold...</i>

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:16.060
<i>Hana.</i>

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.520
<i>Is it warm where you are now?</i>

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.950
<i>Somehow, I'm starting to feel warm.</i>

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.370
<i>It's so warm.</i>

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:44.630
<i>Almost as if Hana were holding me.</i>

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:54.930
<i>Was that a dream?</i>

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:58.220
<i>For some reason, I felt Hana's presence.</i>

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:04.150
<i>I hope that it's nice and warm
wherever she is right now.</i>

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.230
That's right. I'm going to find Hana.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:11.150
I can't let myself die like this.

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:15.240
<i>This is really long.</i>

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:19.370
<i>It's tough too.</i>

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:25.000
<i>Ango, I'm using the knife now.</i>

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:30.760
There we go.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:35.180
Actually, I'll make one more...

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:37.050
...and cover myself with it.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.510
This way, I can avoid being in the sun.

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:41.060
I'll take it slow...

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:43.140
and conserve my energy.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:47.150
<i>It's warm.</i>

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:52.530
<i>I sense Arashi's presence.</i>

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:14.300
It just felt like...

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:17.090
Arashi was here.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:25.480
<i>What are those?</i>

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:28.600
<i>They look like strange rocks.</i>

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:30.860
<i>Are they part of a reef?</i>

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.330
It's only slightly, but I feel it bobbing.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:44.160
This isn't land!

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:47.870
But it seems stable.

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:52.090
For now, this is good news.

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:53.500
I'm saved.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:57.010
<i>That's great, Arashi.</i>

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:00.600
Hana, I want to see you.

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:03.060
Arashi...

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:05.220
I wonder where he is now.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:07.850
Will we ever see each other again?

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:10.770
What should I do?

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:12.900
How do I keep going...

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:14.980
from here on out?

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:21.660
This is Mr. Mark's journal.

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:27.120
<i>After their hopes were crushed</i>

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:31.170
<i>and the chain of disasters
eventually drowned everyone in despair,</i>

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:35.710
<i>how did Mr. Mark and my father react?</i>

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:37.470
<i>How did they continue to survive?</i>

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:42.970
<i>Please, give me an idea.
Tell me what I need to do.</i>

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:46.600
...IS WHAT MR. TAKASHI SAID.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:47.520
<i>Dad?</i>

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:51.690
<i>"After his wife, Ms. Miho, passed away,</i>

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:57.030
<i>I think everything was a lot harder on
Mr. Takashi than any of us could imagine.</i>

00:10:57.740 --> 00:10:59.530
<i>But what was more important to him</i>

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:01.910
<i>was the message
he wanted to leave for his daughter."</i>

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:07.200
If it was possible, I would have liked to
let my daughter know.

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:10.620
Your daughter is alive
somewhere else, right?

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:11.790
Yes.

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:14.250
Then, I'll let her know.

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:18.920
I'll tell her all about how Mr. Takashi,
her father, was brave until the very end.

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:22.130
No, she doesn't need to hear about me.

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:27.140
If you do ever meet my daughter,
please tell her this.

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:32.270
"No matter what kind of world
you wake up in,

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:35.360
please live on
for as long as you possibly can.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:37.570
Just keep living."

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:44.120
Got it. I swear I'll tell her that.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:53.960
"Live on for as long as you possibly can."

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:21.690
<i>Just keep living.</i>

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:26.910
Yes, I already know, Dad.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:31.200
I have to see Arashi again,
no matter what.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:34.120
So, I'm going to live in this world.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:36.460
I'll prove that I can survive.

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:41.300
<i>Fog.</i>

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:43.550
<i>It's like a pure white darkness.</i>

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:48.260
<i>It gently engulfs everything.</i>

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:57.690
<i>When the fog clears,
it leaves drops of water.</i>

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:02.150
<i>I'll gather those up and drink them.</i>

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:08.120
<i>Then when animals come
in search of water, I'll catch them.</i>

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:12.540
Good morning.

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:23.920
<i>I could have eaten
these little guys instead.</i>

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:28.800
<i>But I didn't want to do that.</i>

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:34.060
<i>I think it's okay for me to decide
which of these creatures to eat</i>

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:38.230
<i>based on what my own tastes are.</i>

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:42.020
Where exactly am I right now?

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:45.190
And how did I end up here all alone?

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:56.040
<i>It's no use. I can't remember.</i>

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:58.210
<i>I feel like I don't want to remember.</i>

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:00.250
<i>But why?</i>

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.670
<i>Well, whatever.</i>

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:06.880
I wonder if this is edible.

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:10.930
Don't you think it looks
similar to a rice plant?

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:17.310
Wait! These are all just tiny bugs.

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:21.860
How are they? Yummy?

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:24.940
What?

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:28.400
There are plants growing out of
those bugs over there.

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:30.870
<i>It feels like</i>

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:35.160
<i>I've never stopped to properly look at
my surroundings like this.</i>

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:43.670
<i>I must have thought there was
no good reason to look closely.</i>

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.960
<i>It was all part of a world I didn't like.</i>

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:51.340
The tide is going out.

00:14:56.850 --> 00:15:00.900
<i>Listen, Hana. People assume
there's an abundance of food on land,</i>

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:04.610
<i>but the coast is where
you'll actually find the most.</i>

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:09.110
<i>I'll learn more about this world.</i>

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:13.820
<i>I'll watch carefully
and experience it fully.</i>

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:17.540
What do you want to be
when you grow up, Hana?

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:21.120
An explorer.

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:26.340
Did you hear that, dear?
Hana wants to be an explorer.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.340
Oh, is that so?

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:33.760
Then you'll have to be inquisitive
about many different things.

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:38.930
<i>Right. It's important to be curious.</i>

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:43.940
<i>I'll try exploring outwards
a little further at a time.</i>

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:54.990
An anthill?

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:58.330
They always thrive no matter what era.

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:00.790
They truly are the king of insects.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:03.960
<i>There's a wealth of bugs here.</i>

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:07.040
<i>And plenty of them are edible.</i>

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:10.550
<i>There are also lots of
small mammals hiding around.</i>

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:13.550
<i>I thought I didn't see any flowers,</i>

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:16.140
<i>but on a closer look,
I see a few blooming about.</i>

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:20.390
Hey!

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.520
Hey!

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:28.940
<i>This world is beautiful. It's so exciting!</i>

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:34.200
At first, you will all be
foreign creatures in the future.

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:41.330
Learn and understand the nature
around you, then find your place in it.

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:42.910
Okay.

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:48.380
<i>I suddenly remembered
what Dad once told me.</i>

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:52.920
<i>Back when he told me that,
I was too young to understand.</i>

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:57.180
<i>But now, I think I better understand
what he meant.</i>

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:00.930
What?

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:03.930
You climbed up here? That's dangerous.

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:05.690
Just kidding.

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:09.270
I know you guys have
way better physical abilities than I do.

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:16.780
<i>There's only barren mountains
and brown scrub as far as I can see.</i>

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:20.780
<i>I'd like to start gathering
some fresh water soon.</i>

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:24.040
<i>I wonder where I can find some.</i>

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:28.250
<i>I see something over there.</i>

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:31.500
<i>What are those?</i>

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:34.880
<i>I've never seen
a herd of animals like that.</i>

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:40.180
<i>It's dry season now,
so the dangerous reptiles are hibernating.</i>

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:42.060
<i>It must be easier for them to get around.</i>

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:46.850
<i>But dry-season nights are cold,
so I have to be careful.</i>

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:51.820
It's warm.

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:54.110
It's warm, but...

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:18.630
<i>Is that the herd I saw yesterday?</i>

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:21.720
<i>They came all this way in just one night?</i>

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:33.820
They're so beautiful.

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:39.820
There are colts too.

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:42.570
They're with their mommy,
just like you guys.

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:51.830
They're traveling in search of water.

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:53.590
In that case,

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:54.920
I'm going to follow!

00:18:58.340 --> 00:18:59.510
Goodbye, you guys!

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:04.850
If I find a lot of water,
I'll come back to visit you.

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:07.470
<i>It makes me sad to leave them,</i>

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:10.230
<i>but I know they aren't pets.</i>

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:14.730
<i>My family never kept any animals as pets.</i>

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.570
Here. Use these to take a closer look.

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:18.990
Okay.

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:22.740
What can you see, Hana?

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:27.870
Well, a birdie and a squirrel, I think?

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:34.960
<i>Instead, I got to interact with bugs,
birds, mammals, and fish in the forest.</i>

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:41.130
<i>Both Mom and Dad knew
that I would end up in this situation.</i>

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:51.980
No! Don't worry about me.
I'm not here to eat you or anything.

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:58.650
The mother is looking out for her young.

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:00.320
How adorable.

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:01.400
Time to go.

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:12.330
You go through some pretty crazy terrain.

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:18.250
It's the colt from earlier.

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:22.760
Hey, you, come on now. What are you doing?
Everyone else is leaving.

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:25.800
There'll be trouble if you get separated.
Get moving.

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:26.890
Go!

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:34.520
Go right now! You must not
get separated from your parents!

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:37.110
Jeez!

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:38.070
Sorry about this!

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:43.240
What a relief.

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:46.660
Don't let yourself get separated again.

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:52.660
<i>We're all like a bunch of kids
separated from our parents.</i>

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:56.920
<i>But I don't mind.</i>

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:59.500
<i>I'm totally okay on my own.</i>

00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:06.300
Again?

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:09.050
Hurry up and go join the others!

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:12.060
Wait...

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:15.020
I wonder if you're just not comfortable
being with the others.

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:17.850
Then you're just like me.

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:22.360
<i>Ever since I was a kid,
I've never been good at making friends.</i>

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:24.900
<i>I've never had a best friend either.</i>

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:29.490
<i>The whole time,
I thought that wasn't a flaw of mine,</i>

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:31.330
<i>but it turns out it is.</i>

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:35.000
<i>I always end up disagreeing with people.</i>

00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:37.790
<i>I'm best suited to being alone.</i>

00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:49.680
They finally took a break.
I should get some sleep while I can too.

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:55.390
<i>Even if I don't see Arashi
for a very long time...</i>

00:21:57.600 --> 00:21:58.850
<i>I have to keep on living.</i>

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:03.400
Okay, Arashi!
You can do this! Let's start a fire!

00:22:04.990 --> 00:22:08.530
If I'm going to eat something,
then it's best to cook it.

00:22:08.610 --> 00:22:11.700
It's better than getting sick
and becoming dehydrated.

00:22:13.910 --> 00:22:18.920
<i>Hana, if you saw me now,
you would think I've become a bit tougher.</i>
